  "push_strategy_firebase_label": "Firebase Cloud Messaging",
  "push_strategy_firebase_description": "Instant alerts via Google Firebase. Requires your own Firebase project and a keyfile on the Kuma server.",
  "push_setup_intro": "Choose how you want to receive alerts when a monitor goes down.",
  "push_setup_alert_subtext": "Alert when monitors go down or recover",
  "push_setup_background_checks_hint": "Background checks run every 15 minutes when the app is closed",
  "push_setup_delivery_method_section": "Delivery Method",
  "push_setup_more_methods_coming": "More methods coming soon",
  "push_setup_no_distributor_badge": "No distributor",
  "push_setup_not_built_in_badge": "Not built in",
  "push_setup_ntfy_how_title": "How ntfy works",
  "push_setup_ntfy_how_body": "This app keeps one persistent connection open to the ntfy server (a background service with an ongoing notification) and listens for messages published to your topic. Uptime Kuma pushes to that topic the instant it detects a change, so alerts arrive immediately instead of waiting for a periodic check.\n\nRequires a matching ntfy notification provider configured in Uptime Kuma itself, using the same topic (and server, if self-hosted).\n\nTrade-off: keeps a connection running at all times (which shows a persistent notification). If you already use the ntfy app for other things, UnifiedPush avoids running a second one.",
  "push_setup_setup_label": "Setup",
  "push_setup_ntfy_setup_steps": "1. Pick a unique topic name\n2. In Uptime Kuma → Notifications → add ntfy provider\n3. Enter the same topic and server URL",
  "push_setup_ntfy_server_label": "ntfy Server",
  "push_setup_ntfy_topic_label": "Topic",
  "push_setup_ntfy_topic_support": "Must match your Uptime Kuma ntfy notification config",
  "push_setup_ntfy_auth_optional": "Authentication (optional)",
  "push_setup_ntfy_access_token_label": "Access Token",
  "push_setup_save_connect": "Save & Connect",
  "push_setup_test": "Test",
  "push_setup_up_how_title": "How UnifiedPush works",
  "push_setup_up_how_body": "Delegates the always-on connection to whichever UnifiedPush distributor you have installed (the ntfy app, Gotify, NextPush, etc.). That app holds one shared connection on behalf of every UnifiedPush-enabled app on your phone, so this app keeps nothing running in the background itself. When a message arrives, the OS briefly wakes this app just long enough to show the alert.\n\nOnce registered, you'll get an endpoint URL to paste into Uptime Kuma as a webhook notification.\n\nTrade-off: needs a UnifiedPush distributor app already installed. Most battery-friendly option when one is.",
  "push_setup_registered": "Registered",
  "push_setup_endpoint_url_label": "Endpoint URL",
  "push_setup_copy_endpoint_url": "Copy Endpoint URL",
  "push_setup_setup_in_kuma": "Setup in Uptime Kuma",
  "push_setup_up_setup_steps": "1. Copy the endpoint URL above\n2. In Uptime Kuma → Notifications → add a Webhook notification\n3. Paste the endpoint URL as the webhook URL\n4. Set Content Type to application/json\n5. Test and save",
  "push_setup_up_registering": "Registering with distributor...",
  "push_setup_retry": "Retry",
  "push_setup_select_distributor": "Select a distributor:",
  "push_setup_no_distributor_found": "No UnifiedPush distributor found",
  "push_setup_install_distributor_hint": "Install a distributor app like ntfy, Gotify, or NextPush from F-Droid or your app store, then come back here.",
  "push_setup_firebase_not_configured": "This build isn't set up for Firebase",
  "push_setup_firebase_not_configured_hint": "Firebase needs google-services.json bundled at build time.",
  "push_setup_firebase_registering": "Registering with Firebase...",
  "push_setup_device_token_label": "Device Token",
  "push_setup_copy_device_token": "Copy Device Token",
  "push_setup_register_firebase": "Register with Firebase",
  "push_setup_firebase_setup_title": "Setup is more involved than the other options",
  "push_setup_firebase_setup_steps": "Uptime Kuma has no built-in Firebase provider and reaches Firebase through its bundled Apprise integration, which needs credentials on the Kuma server itself, not this app.\n\n1. Create a Firebase project (console.firebase.google.com)\n2. Project Settings → Service Accounts → Generate new private key — this downloads a JSON keyfile\n3. Put that keyfile somewhere the Kuma server can read it (e.g. a mounted volume in its Docker container)\n4. In Uptime Kuma → Notifications → add an Apprise notification with this URL:\n   fcm://{ProjectID}/{DeviceToken}/?keyfile=/path/to/keyfile.json\n   — using your Firebase Project ID and the device token above\n\nNote: deep-linking to a specific monitor isn't available through this path since Kuma/Apprise don't pass structured monitor data so tapping a Firebase alert opens the dashboard. Also, Android auto-displays these with default styling when the app is backgrounded (a general FCM behavior); custom styling only applies while the app is in the foreground.",
  "push_setup_pull_how_title": "How polling works",
  "push_setup_pull_how_body": "A background task runs every 15 minutes (Android's minimum), connects to your Uptime Kuma instance via Socket.IO, checks all monitor statuses, and sends a notification if anything changed since the last check.\n\nNo additional server-side setup is needed besides your Uptime Kuma URL and credentials.\n\nTrade-off: alerts can be delayed up to 15 minutes. For instant alerts, switch to ntfy or UnifiedPush.",
  "push_setup_ntfy_status_connected": "Connected: listening for alerts",
